    "result_text": "The build is green with all tests passing. Here's what I implemented for the version-2 owner identity release.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 \u2014 every identifier changes, no V1 value recurs)**\n- Added a fixed `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` on `Owner`.\n- `Owner.getIdentityKey()` now hashes `\"V2|\" + telephone + \"|\" + email + \"|\" + soundex(lastName)` \u2014 duplicate-detection semantics preserved, value changed.\n- `householdIdFor()` (controller) now hashes `\"V2|\" + normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` \u2014 household grouping preserved (still a pure function of last name + postcode), value changed.\n- `memberIdFor()` now uses a new `identityRegion()` = `\"V2\" + postcodeRegion` (e.g. `V2NSW`, `V2UNKNOWN`) as the `<REGION>` segment, so the member id becomes e.g. `V2NSW2716E6609E7`.\n\n**User-facing region stays plain (no `V2` tag)**\n- `locality()` no longer parses the region out of the memberId (which now carries `V2`); it resolves the plain region directly from postcode \u2192 city table (`NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`/`UNKNOWN`).\n- `fiscalYear()` now derives `FY<YY>` directly from `registrationDate` instead of parsing the memberId.\n- `timezone` and `ownerSegment` derive from the plain `locality`, so their region never carries the tag (confirmed: `ownerSegment=STANDARD_METRO` for an NSW owner).\n\n**Response shape**\n- OpenAPI: removed top-level `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey`; added an `OwnerIdentity` schema and grouped the three under a nested `identity` object; added a top-level integer `apiVersion` (2).\n- Mapper populates `identity(owner)` and `apiVersion = 2`.\n\n**Audit event \u2192 schema v2**\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` gained `schemaVersion` (2) and `ownerSegment` (recomputed from the V2 identity pipeline). Emitted JSON: `{\"schemaVersion\":2,\"seq\":1,...,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW...\",\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
