    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered trace of `addOwner` (the handler for `POST /api/owners`), covering every validation (V) and side-effect (S) in the order they execute. Line references are to `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n## Before the method body\n\n1. **(V) Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (line 608): caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else the call is rejected.\n2. **(V) Bean validation of the request body** \u2014 the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner` binds the body as a validated `OwnerFieldsDto`, so Spring's Bean Validation runs on it before the body executes.\n\n## Idempotency short-circuit\n\n3. **(S/V) Idempotency lookup** (lines 614\u2013623): reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was already used and the owner still exists, it returns that original owner with **200 OK** and does nothing else (no new create).\n\n## Mapping + field validations\n\n4. **(S) Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (line 624): `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`.\n5. **(V) Postcode validity** (lines 625\u2013628, `isPostcodeValid`): postcode is optional; if present it must be exactly 4 digits and, when the city maps to a known region, fall within that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Else **400**.\n6. **(V) Telephone** (lines 629\u2013633): normalized to E.164 via `toE164`; must be non-null and pass `hasValidNationalLength`. Else **400**. (The normalized value is applied later at step 9.)\n7. **(V + S) Email** (lines 634\u2013637, `normalizeEmail`): mutates the owner \u2014 blank \u2192 null; otherwise must match the email regex and not be on the disposable-domain blocklist, and is lower-cased in place. Invalid \u2192 **400**.\n8. **(V + S) Address composition** (lines 638\u2013643, `composeAddress`): prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (normalized in place \u2014 trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, street abbreviations expanded), else normalizes the flat `address`. If nothing yields a non-empty address \u2192 **400**; otherwise `owner.setAddress(composed)`.\n9. **(S) Apply normalized telephone** (line 644): `owner.setTelephone(e164)`.\n10. **(V) Registration date not in the future** (lines 645\u2013649): if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today \u2192 **400**.\n\n## Rate / capacity limits\n\n11. **(S, internal) Business-day-adjusted registration date** (lines 650\u2013651): effective date defaults to today if absent, then rolls forward off weekends/public holidays (`toBusinessDay`).\n12. **(V) Daily create limit** (lines 652\u2013656): if owners already registered on that business day \u2265 100 \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**.\n13. **(V) City capacity** (lines 657\u2013661): if existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2265 50 \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n\n## Household / identity computation\n\n14. **(S) Set householdId** (line 665): deterministic SHA-256 over `V2|normalizedLastName|postcode`.\n15. **(S, internal) Compute household members & flags** (lines 666\u2013668): existing same-household owners, plus the caller-declared `sharesHousehold` flag.\n16. **(V) Hard duplicate** (lines 675\u2013684): if any non-deleted existing owner has the same `identityKey` (SHA-256 over telephone|email|soundex(lastName)) \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n17. **(S) Possible-duplicate flagging** (lines 693\u2013701): if a declared household member, sets `possibleDuplicate=false` / `possibleDuplicateOf=null`; otherwise looks up a soundex+postcode soft match and sets `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` accordingly.\n18. **(S) Set namesakeCount** (line 702): count of existing owners with same first+last name.\n19. **(S) Set householdSize** (line 703): household members + 1.\n20. **(S) Set membershipLevelCap** (lines 706\u2013715): null if no existing household members, else max household membership level + 1.\n21. **(S) Set bulkSignupWarning** (line 716): true if owners already registered that day > 80.\n22. **(S) Set c